WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.502
-Thank you very much, everyone!
Thank you!

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:05.905
Welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.507
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:11.344
Well, guys, it is a big night
for the country

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.579
as Georgia held
its two runoff elections,

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:16.750
which will determine the balance
of power in the Senate.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:20.152
It was exciting this morning
when MSNBC pried open the lid

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:23.256
and watched Steve Kornacki arise
from his hyperbaric chamber.

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:24.657
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:28.394
"The Kornak is back
wearing the khak!"

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:30.663
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.532
Because these races
are so important,

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.900
last night President Trump
traveled to Georgia and held

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.670
a rally on behalf of
the two Republican candidates,

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.406
Senator David Perdue
and Kelly Loeffler.

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:41.640
Yep, it was quite a night.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.843
Trump spoke for
almost 90 minutes,

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.078
and then he invited everyone
on a scavenger hunt

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:47.847
to find 12,000 more votes.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.615
[ Laughter ]
That was nice.

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:52.518
Yeah, the whole point of Trump's
visit was to rally support

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:54.153
for the two Republican
candidates,

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.721
but GOP officials were worried

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:58.023
he'd start talking about
his loss to Biden.

00:00:58.023 --> 00:01:00.159
Let's see how long
he stayed on message.

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:03.029 line:0%
-I want to thank you very much.
Hello, Georgia.

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:06.065 line:0%
By the way, there's no way
we lost Georgia.

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.567 line:0%
There's no way.
-Ah!

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.302
Five seconds. Well, way longer
than I expected.

00:01:10.302 --> 00:01:11.904
Trump would read
"A Tale of Two Cities"

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:14.373
like, "It was the best of --
By the way, I am the best.

00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:16.809
Everyone says I'm the best."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:19.178
Seriously, he's still
campaigning for an election

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:21.114
he already lost.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.216
Imagine Justin Guarini
tweeting today,

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:26.319
"Text 50815 and make me
the next American Idol."

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:30.189
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:32.592
It's been a while since Trump
made a campaign speech.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:33.860
And he seemed a little rusty.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.096
Listen closely to how he
pronounced the word America.

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:41.167
-We have made "Uhmeruca"
strong again.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.268
Look at that arm.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.771
-What happened?
W-W-What happened there?

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.574
It was like halfway through
a hypnotist put him to sleep.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:48.641
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.076
"We have made --"
Sleep!

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:54.747
"Uhmeruca strong again."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.282
"Is there ice in my shoe?"

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.550
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.986
[ Clucks ]
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.754
It was either that
or one of his aides

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.456
hit him with a tranq dart.

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.558
"Uhmeruca."

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:08.328
Can we see it again there, Dave,
Uhmeruca?

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:12.431
-We have made Uhmeruca
strong again.

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:13.599
Look at that arm.

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:16.069
-"Look at that arm."
Distraction.

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.103
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.337
If he can't say America,

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:20.306
why can't he just go
with the United States?

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:23.108
-God bless the United Shtates.

00:02:23.108 --> 00:02:26.712
-Ah. That's why. That's why.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:28.381
Another big moment
during the speech was

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.850
when Trump brought up
Vice President Pence.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.318
Yeah, Trump has been begging
Pence to stop Congress

00:02:33.318 --> 00:02:36.122
from certifying the Electoral
College vote tomorrow.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.857
Pence can't really do that,

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.426
but that hasn't stopped Trump
from pressuring him.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:44.096
-I hope Mike Pence comes through
for us, I have to tell you.

00:02:44.096 --> 00:02:46.132
He's a great guy.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:48.400
Of course if he doesn't
come through,

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.570
I won't like him quite as much.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.238
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:55.341
-Pence's only role is to preside
over the ballot counting.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:58.578
He's basically one step
above a bingo caller.

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:01.347
Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.850
That's a respected profession
in this crowd.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:07.119
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:09.188
Bingo caller not that bad.

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:11.223
We like bingo caller.

00:03:11.223 --> 00:03:12.458
He's the vice president.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:15.661
Yeah. Mm.

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:17.897
Bingo caller.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.965
Yeah, Trump said he hopes
Mike Pence

00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:21.567
comes through tomorrow

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.135
and basically overturns
the election.

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:25.638
-Wait, wait, wait,
Trump wants Mike Pence

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:28.141
to swoop in
and overturn the results?

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:30.275
-Yeah, Mike Pence.

00:03:30.275 --> 00:03:32.912
-Mr. Bore?
-Senior Snore.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:35.414
-Dr. Doh?
-McDreary.

00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:38.050
-Christian Pale?
-Ashen Kutcher.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:41.453
-Android Cuomo?
-Robot de Niro.

00:03:41.453 --> 00:03:42.988
[ Laughter ]
-Pence help?

00:03:42.988 --> 00:03:44.724
-Hell no.
-Biden win?

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.358
-Once again.
-That's cool.

00:03:46.358 --> 00:03:47.927
-That's right.
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.595
-Yep, yep.
-New Year's?

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:51.064
-Not bad.
-Gold plates?

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:52.799
-Stay at home?
-Champagne.

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:54.833
-Oh, yeah.
-Dom bomb?

00:03:54.833 --> 00:03:56.402
-Cheap stuff.
-Headache?

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:58.270
-Real bad.
-Sorry, man.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.039
-All good.
-Cool, cool.

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:03.909
Good talk.

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:05.912
-Best buds?
-Uh, do the monologue.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:11.183
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.183 --> 00:04:12.885
-Right.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.887
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:17.256
Meanwhile, during the trip
to Georgia, Ivanka Trump

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:21.427
tweeted a photo from Marine One
and accidently tagged the singer

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:27.966
Meat Loaf instead of her father.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.966 --> 00:04:30.035
Secret Service was like,
"Ivanka, please, please,

00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:32.138
don't give away his code name."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:35.007
Yep, Ivanka tried to tag
@realdonaldtrump

00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:37.477
but accidently ended up
with @realmeatloaf.

00:04:37.477 --> 00:04:38.678
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.779
In response Arby's was like,
"That's funny.

00:04:40.779 --> 00:04:43.049
There's no such thing
as real meatloaf."

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:44.550
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.419
Listen to this.
I read that the CEO of

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:49.288
Whole Foods, John Mackey,
is being criticized

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:51.790
after saying healthcare
would not be necessary

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:55.194
if people would eat better
and live healthier lifestyles.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.995
Can't wait till
John breaks his leg

00:04:56.995 --> 00:04:59.766
and the ER doctor prescribes him
a $20 mango.

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:02.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:04.136
Some entertainment news --
last night was

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:06.138
the season premiere
of "The Bachelor."

00:05:06.138 --> 00:05:09.408
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:05:09.408 --> 00:05:12.011
And the most talked about moment
was the arrival

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:15.148
of a woman who brought Matt
an interesting gift.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:16.482
Watch this.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:17.883
-I brought something
from home...

00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:19.919
-Okay.
-...that's really special to me.

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:22.288
This pandemic was really hard
for me.

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:25.091
And this just really got me
through a lot.

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:28.127
And I was hoping to pass the
torch to you.

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:36.468
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.468 --> 00:05:38.771
-Who knew the naked dodgeball
season would end up

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:41.206
being the "classy" season?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.206 --> 00:05:43.609
Then Chris Harrison was like,
"She's not a contestant.

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:44.710
I don't know how that lady
got in there.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.512
Please wash your hands, please."

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:49.415
It'll be awkward in 10 years
when their kids are like,

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:52.018
"Mom, Dad, tell us about
when you first met."

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:53.819
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.819 --> 00:05:56.389
Just a reminder
that ABC is owned by Disney.

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:59.091
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.091 --> 00:06:01.293
People tune in like, "It'll be
nice to take a break

00:06:01.293 --> 00:06:03.228
from all the horrible news
and just -- okay, you know what?

00:06:03.228 --> 00:06:05.064
Back to CNN, let's put on CNN."

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:09.201
Eh.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:11.937
And finally, a company that
makes face masks for pets

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:16.642
has seen a 500% increase in
sales since the pandemic began.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.644
Here's a dog wearing
one of the masks.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.481
Meanwhile, dogs
are going to be like,

00:06:22.481 --> 00:06:24.217
"It's not COVID.
It's my breath, isn't it?"

